#Live Bus Tracking 
## Abstract

The Live Bus Tracking System is a real-time transportation management system developed to help passengers track the current location of buses. The system uses GPS technology to collect the bus location and displays it on a map, allowing users to easily identify the bus position and estimate its arrival time. This reduces passenger waiting time and provides convenient access to transportation information. The system can also help drivers and transport authorities monitor bus movements and manage routes effectively. Overall, the Live Bus Tracking System provides a simple, efficient, and user-friendly solution for improving public transportation services.
